      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name}\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n1. Download any English ASCII font (I am testing with BoldPixels https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/2d/fonts/boldpixels-font-332078).\n\n2. Open Font Asset Creator: In Unity, Window > TextMeshPro > Font Asset Creator.\n\n3. Configure;\n\n    • Select the downloaded font as the source font.\n\n    • Set the Character Set to ASCII.\n\n    • Click Generate Font Atlas and save the new font asset.\n\n4. Create a new TextMeshPro object via GameObject > UI > Text - TextMeshPro (VRC). (should spawn with a canvas, if not make one)\n\n5. Assign the newly created custom font asset to this text object.\n\n6. Type or paste non-ASCII characters (e.g., こんにちは) into the text field.\n\nReproduction World:\n\nHere is a test world with 2 canvases, one set to BoldPixels and the other set to LiberationSans SDF https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_d5e463e3-0630-4b2f-86b1-a1c5c3539a4d/info",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
