  "details": "When using a custom Font Asset after the Unity 6 update, missing glyphs (such as Korean characters) no longer correctly utilise fallback fonts. Instead, they render as missing block characters. If the built-in default LiberationSans SDF is used, the fallback mechanism works as intended.\n\nI have tested multiple fallback configurations, none of which resolved the issue:\n\n• Linking LiberationSans SDF explicitly as a fallback inside the custom Font Asset.\n\n• Linking it in the TextMeshPro Project Settings.\n\n• Leaving all fallback fields empty to let VRChat's system handle the fallback behaviour.\n\nAttached Files:\n\n• Image 1 & 2: Expected behaviour before the Unity 6 update (English and Korean glyphs rendering properly).\n\n• Image 3: Current broken behaviour after the update (All non-ASCII text converted into blocks).",
